"Weak" is a relative term. I, personally, would never call a person who
ascends in standard mode without scumsaving "weak", even if they've
only done it once.

YAFAP is a proud accomplishment that sometimes takes years to achieve.
To my mind Nethack is much like a marathon .. while there is only one
person who finishes first everyone who runs the 26 miles has something
to be proud of.  Calling a runner "weak" because they placed 121st
instead of 2nd or 3rd completely ignores their main accomplishment,
which is to finish a race most people won't even attempt.

Certainly a player that ascends without using the E-word is more
skillful than someone who does.  But that doesn't make the second
player "weak", anymore than an olympic athlete is a couch potato if he
doesn't win any medals.  

